# Production / cloud wiring gate

When the user asks to **wire cloud**, **connect APIs**, **deploy**, **GCP/GKE/Terraform**, **infra**, **third-party keys**, or **is this production-ready** — analyze the **codebase first**. Do not start cloud work because a plan or matrix looks complete.

## YES to cloud wiring only if ALL are true (proved this session)

1. **Product spine works in code** — order → dispatch → payload/driver → pay-at-delivery → fiscal/settlement (or the product's real spine) is REAL, not THEATRE, on the claimed path.
2. **Data plane** — mutations use durable SoT (Spanner RW + same-txn outbox, not memory/`Apply` theatre). Consumers and WS fanout exist for user-visible state.
3. **All shipped role-row clients** call the live API (or are explicitly deferred in code comments + ledger, not silently missing).
4. **Tests** — unit + integration (or SSMR/CI-equivalent) for the spine are green **after** a re-read of the edited files.
5. Remaining work is **secrets, env, DNS, IAM** — not new product logic.

If any item fails → **NO**. List blockers ranked. Offer the next **code** phase, not a cloud checklist.

## Hard split

| Layer A (code) | Layer B (cloud) |
|---|---|
| State machines, clients, events, honesty of empty/error | GSM secrets, PSP/OFD keys, GKE, Terraform apply |

Cloud day must not invent features. If connecting a key would require new business logic, **you are not ready**.

